# Carom — Showcase

The finished game ships a showcase: the store-page presentation of the game, in
a `showcase/` directory at the root of this repository. This file defines its
contents.

## Layout

Every file of the showcase sits directly in `showcase/`, with no subdirectories:

| Path | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `showcase/showcase.md` | The description. |
| `showcase/showcase.toml` | The carousel. |
| `showcase/<file>` | Each media file the carousel and the description name. |

## The description

`showcase/showcase.md` is Markdown written for a player: what Carom is, how a
match plays out from the opening rally to match point, and how its spin and bank
shots feel in play. Three to five short paragraphs, with playing the game as
their whole subject. It may embed images that sit beside it, referenced by bare
relative path (for example `![The field](field.png)`); every image it embeds is a
`.png` in `showcase/`.

## The carousel

`showcase/showcase.toml` lists the media in the order they are presented, one
`[[media]]` table per entry:

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
```toml
[[media]]
file = "rally.webm"
name = "A rally curving through the obstacles"

[[media]]
file = "title.png"
name = "The title screen"
```
{{else}}
```toml
[[media]]
file = "rally.json.gz"
name = "A rally curving through the obstacles"

[[media]]
file = "title.png"
name = "The title screen"
```
{{/if}}

- `file` names a file directly in `showcase/`, with no path separators. Every
  file the carousel names is present there, and each stays under 25 MiB.
- `name` is a caption of a few words.
- The carousel holds two to four entries, and the first is the strongest view of
  live play.

## Media

The file extension states what an entry is:

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
| Extension | Media |
| --- | --- |
| `.png` | A screenshot of the running game. |
| `.webm` | A video clip of the running game, a few seconds long. |

Screenshots carry most of the carousel. Motion, such as spin curving a flight
into a bank shot, ships as a `.webm` clip. How screenshots and clips are captured
is yours to decide.
{{else}}
| Extension | Media |
| --- | --- |
| `.png` | A screenshot of the running game. |
| `.json.gz` | A replay: a gzipped recording of the game's own drawing, made with the engine's recorder, which the engine documents in `engine/recording.md`. |

Screenshots carry most of the carousel. Motion ships as a replay, and each replay
holds a few seconds of live play, such as a rally banking through the obstacles.
How screenshots and replays are captured is yours to decide.
{{/if}}
